    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_premise",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The conclusion sounds reasonable only because an unstated premise treats efficiency as more important than equity."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نتیجه فقط به این دلیل منطقی به نظر میاد که یک پیش‌فرض ناگفته کارایی رو مهم‌تر از عدالت فرض کرده."
        },
        "intent": "surface_hidden_premise",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_premise",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_inference"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_validity",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The argument may be logically valid while still being unpersuasive if one of its central premises is poorly supported."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "استدلال ممکنه از نظر منطقی معتبر باشه ولی اگر یکی از مقدمات اصلیش پشتوانه ضعیفی داشته باشه همچنان قانع‌کننده نباشه."
        },
        "intent": "separate_validity_support",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_validity",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_premise"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_soundness",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "For the argument to be sound, we need both valid reasoning and premises that are actually credible."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "برای اینکه استدلال واقعاً درست و محکم باشه، هم منطق معتبر می‌خوایم و هم مقدماتی که واقعاً قابل اعتماد باشن."
        },
        "intent": "define_soundness",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_soundness",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_validity"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_fallacy",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "Calling the disagreement a false choice is useful only if we can show a realistic third option rather than merely naming a fallacy."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "گفتن اینکه بحث دوگانه‌سازی کاذبه فقط وقتی مفیده که واقعاً گزینه سوم عملی نشون بدیم، نه اینکه فقط اسم مغالطه رو بگیم."
        },
        "intent": "diagnose_fallacy",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_fallacy",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_rebuttal"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_circular",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The justification is circular: the policy is described as necessary because it is said to be unavoidable, and unavoidable because it is necessary."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "توجیه دوریه: سیاست ضروریه چون اجتناب‌ناپذیره و اجتناب‌ناپذیره چون ضروریه."
        },
        "intent": "identify_circularity",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_circular",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_premise"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_burden",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The burden of proof lies with the stronger claim, especially when it asks us to overturn a well-supported default assumption."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "بار اثبات با ادعای قوی‌تره، مخصوصاً وقتی می‌خواد یک فرض پیش‌فرض با پشتوانه خوب رو کنار بزنه."
        },
        "intent": "assign_burden_of_proof",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_burden_of_proof",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_inference"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_rebuttal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "A strong rebuttal addresses the best version of the opposing argument rather than the easiest version to attack."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "یک پاسخ استدلالی قوی به بهترین نسخه حرف طرف مقابل جواب می‌ده، نه ساده‌ترین نسخه‌ای که می‌شه بهش حمله کرد."
        },
        "intent": "construct_rebuttal",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_rebuttal",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_soundness"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_argument_diagnostics_summary",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Before accepting the conclusion, trace the inference, expose the premises and ask which step carries the greatest evidential burden."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "قبل از قبول نتیجه، مسیر استنتاج رو دنبال کن، پیش‌فرض‌ها رو آشکار کن و ببین کدوم مرحله بیشترین بار شواهدی رو داره."
        },
        "intent": "diagnose_argument",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_inference",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_premise",
          "c2_argument_diagnostics_burden_of_proof"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_argument_diagnostics_concession_rebuttal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-01",
        "slug": "c2-argument-diagnostics-concession-rebuttal",
        "title": "Concession followed by rebuttal",
        "rule_summary": "Acknowledge a reasonable opposing point before limiting it or presenting a stronger counterargument.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "ابتدا یک نکته منطقی از طرف مقابل را می‌پذیریم و سپس دامنه آن را محدود می‌کنیم یا پاسخ قوی‌تری می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Granted, the process is faster; that does not necessarily make it fairer.",
            "fa": "درست است که روند سریع‌تر است؛ اما لزوماً عادلانه‌تر نیست."
          },
          {
            "en": "While that concern is valid, it overlooks the cost of doing nothing.",
            "fa": "با اینکه آن نگرانی معتبر است، هزینه هیچ کاری نکردن را نادیده می‌گیرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_argument_diagnostics_cleft_sentences",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-02",
        "slug": "c2-argument-diagnostics-cleft-sentences",
        "title": "Cleft sentences for focus",
        "rule_summary": "Use what-clauses and it-clefts to place deliberate emphasis on the most important part of a message.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با what-clause و it-cleft بخش مهم پیام را برجسته می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "What concerns me most is the lack of independent oversight.",
            "fa": "چیزی که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند نبود نظارت مستقل است."
          },
          {
            "en": "It was the timing, rather than the decision itself, that caused the problem.",
            "fa": "زمان‌بندی بود، نه خود تصمیم، که مشکل را ایجاد کرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_argument_diagnostics_discourse_management",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-03",
        "slug": "c2-argument-diagnostics-discourse-management",
        "title": "Managing complex discourse",
        "rule_summary": "Use signposting and metadiscourse to frame, sequence, return to, and close complex points without losing the listener.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با signposting و metadiscourse نکات پیچیده را قاب‌بندی، مرتب، دوباره جمع و نتیجه‌گیری می‌کنیم تا شنونده مسیر بحث را گم نکند."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Before I come back to that point, let me clarify one assumption.",
            "fa": "قبل از اینکه به آن نکته برگردم، بگذار یک فرض را روشن کنم."
          },
          {
            "en": "That brings us to the broader question of accountability.",
            "fa": "این ما را به پرسش گسترده‌تر پاسخ‌گویی می‌رساند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c2_argument_diagnostics_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-argument-diagnostics-01",
        "title": "Argument Diagnostics & Hidden Premises: part 1",
        "setting": "seminar break",
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "characters": [
          "Ella",
          "Amir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Ella",
            "text": "Which assumption is doing most of the work here?",
            "translation_fa": "کدوم فرض بیشترین نقش رو در این استدلال داره؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Amir",
            "text": "The conclusion sounds reasonable only because an unstated premise treats efficiency as more important than equity.",
            "translation_fa": "نتیجه فقط به این دلیل منطقی به نظر میاد که یک پیش‌فرض ناگفته کارایی رو مهم‌تر از عدالت فرض کرده."
